## 5. Repo hygiene

`.gitignore` had `docs/sphinx/_build/`, but Sphinx output lives at
`documentation/sphinx/_build/`. The rule never matched, so **330 files / 46MB of
generated HTML were committed** — including pages for modules P5 deleted
(`SyncedTableManager.html`, `LakebaseFlatStore.html`). It also poisoned every
`grep` over the docs, which is what made the original audit so noisy.

Added the correct path and untracked the tree (`git rm -r --cached`; files stay on
disk). CI rebuilds it with `make html`, so nothing is lost. The `docs/` rule was
left alone — that directory exists and is separate.

Also deleted `documentation/sphinx/api/app.core.graphdb.lakebase.rst`, whose every
`automodule` pointed at `back.core.graphdb.lakebase.*` — a package that no longer
exists — and replaced it with `app.core.graphdb.postgres.rst` against the real
modules. The toctree was retargeted and every entry in it now verified to resolve.

